  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0. **Stacked on #1080** (#982, itself stacked on #1007): the diff against `main` shows their commits too; this PR's own change is the last commit (`budget.rs`, `budget_twins.rs`, `grow.rs`, one line of `lib.rs`, `rotary_adaptive.rs`, the decision file). The twins need #1080's `rings::OPEN_INSET` hook, its level reader and its microlift fix - on main the same levels flip to \"refused for travel\" on the lift edge once the budget lets them through.\n\n## What the knife edge was\n\nNot the limits. The growth planner (`adaptive/grow.rs`) grows an area from a wall margin that closes 2.5 um a revolution; where the margin is spent before the fronts are done (about 140 revolutions at the first rung) the whole plan is made again from a wider margin (`MARGIN_SCALES` 1.0, 1.6, 2.4). Whether a plan needing about 140 revolutions finishes inside the first margin or just after is a matter of nanometres. The #850 budgets were **summed over the attempts**, so \"ran out of margin\" also meant \"the retry starts with a whole attempt already spent\" - the sum jumped by 22.5 k tool radii on an 8 nm change.\n\nThe r7 bar's developed level at radius 5.0 (release, Linux x86-64):\n\n| openings deeper by | first attempt | second attempt | before (summed) | now (per attempt) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0, 8, 16, 32, 510 nm | runs out of margin at 22.5 k r, 377-380 k vertices | done in 24.5-24.7 k r, 396-400 k vertices | refused at 30 k r, 85-86 revolutions into the retry; rings | HSM-planned |\n| 62, 125, 250 nm | done in 22.3 k r, 375-377 k vertices | - | HSM-planned | HSM-planned |\n\nThe window's levels 6.0 and 5.0 are the same band and the same case (first attempt done at 8, 125 and 250 nm).\n\n## What changed\n\n- `adaptive/budget.rs`: laws 2 (30 k r) and 3 (600 k vertices past 5 k r) are counted for each margin attempt on its own - `Work::attempt()` resets the sums, called at the top of `Planner::grow`. Limits, law 1 and every refusal text are unchanged.\n- Counted per attempt, a sum moved by at most 0.7 % (length) and 1.6 % (vertices) over every perturbation tried; the nearest attempt on our fixtures is 24.7 k of 30 k r (1.21x under) and 400 k of 600 k vertices (1.50x under), pinned as margins.\n- The \"never hang\" bound is now three attempts of 30 k r (the ladder's three rungs) instead of 30 k r in all. Only a plan that runs out of margin uses more than one attempt; law 3 still stops a heavy plan inside its first. The bar's level 5.0: ~11 s to be refused before, ~14 s to be planned now.\n\n## Verdicts that change\n\n- `rotary_adaptive`, r7 bar, level 5.0: was \"refused past the budget\", cut by rings at a full-width load (13 breaks); now HSM-planned (8545 planar moves, 1935 arcs, 18.4 % D, no in-cut break past 5 degrees). The pin names 6.5, 6.0, 5.5, 5.0 as planned and forbids a budget refusal.\n- `rotary_adaptive`, window, levels 6.0 and 5.0: were refused past the budget; now HSM-planned (18.8 % D, no break). Pinned the same way.\n- Nothing else: across every motion suite and the app suites that plan Adaptive (release, `--include-ignored`) no other plan reaches a second margin attempt; every other refusal (the island at 109 revolutions / 600 037 vertices / 9.4 k r, the stepped block, the bands refused up front) falls inside its first attempt with the same counts. No golden file moves.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `adaptive::budget::tests::each_margin_attempt_is_held_to_the_budget_on_its_own` (default suite).\n- `adaptive::budget::twins::the_r7_bars_levels_decide_the_same_way_under_sub_micron_perturbations` and `...::the_windows_levels_decide_the_same_way_under_sub_micron_perturbations` (heavy lane, release `--ignored`, ~100 s together): openings 0, 8, 16, 62, 250 nm deeper; every level under the skin HSM-planned in every twin, no budget refusal, no planner overload, load within the suite's law, each attempt within the stated margins. Both are red at 0 nm without the change.\n- `rotary_adaptive::adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws` and `::the_developed_window_reaches_the_planner_and_names_each_refusal` now state the levels' verdicts.\n- The existing budget refusal fixtures are unchanged and green (`budget::fixtures`, `adaptive_hsm`'s island, motion and app `pocket3d_hsm`).\n- On the final head 5516dbc3: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/982-microlift-acceptance` green (motion lib, adaptive_band, adaptive_hsm, adaptive_orbit_seam, pocket3d_hsm; 0 failed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; release `--include-ignored`: motion lib 201/201, rotary_adaptive 6/6, adaptive_hsm 6/6, adaptive_band 2/2, adaptive_orbit_seam 1/1, motion pocket3d_hsm 4/4, app pocket3d_hsm 2/2, pick_agnostic 7/7, shoulder_adaptive 3/3. Before the change was final, every motion test (`--include-ignored`, release) and every app suite that mentions Adaptive ran green with a probe that printed each margin attempt.\n\n## Not settled here / not exercised\n\n- Which margin a plan is made from still turns on nanometres, so the twins post different plans (all HSM, all within the load law). On the r7 bar's level 5.0 the plan made inside the first margin (62, 125, 250 nm) posts 5 in-cut breaks of 5.0-6.2 degrees at the band's end; the wider-margin plan (0, 8, 16, 32, 510 nm, the unperturbed bar among them) posts none. Those are #1050's end kinks, present on main whenever the first margin suffices; this change newly accepts only the wider-margin plan. The twins hold level 5.0 to at most 5 (`BAR_50_BREAKS`, to go with #1050) and the unperturbed bar to none. Making the plans alike, not only the verdicts, is #882's.\n- Only Linux x86-64 was measured; another platform's libm puts the margin edge at other nanometres (the twins cover both sides here).\n- The batch and release tiers and the UI suites were not run (motion only is touched).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1051-planning-budget-edge.md`.\n\nChangelog: Adaptive: the planning budget is held per margin attempt, so a level is no longer refused (and cut by Offset rings) or HSM-planned depending on nanometre-scale geometry; the rotary r7 bar's level 5.0 and the window's levels 6.0 / 5.0 are now HSM-planned.\n\nEffort: max (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1051\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
